  "changes": [
    {
      "area": "transform-agnostic output boundary",
      "result": "Any validated nonempty SecretArg or SecretEnv now establishes one immutable invocation sensitivity before Command construction and before either output pipe exists. Both streams use a withholding collector that never retains, hashes, counts, or serializes subprocess bytes; no literal, prefix, encoding, or transform matcher participates in declassification."
    },
    {
      "area": "caller-controlled invocation metadata",
      "result": "Secret-bearing runs now omit reversible public argument values, environment names and values, secret-source names and versions, cwd paths, and worktree enforcement scopes from JSON and Debug. Records retain only a stable withheld disposition, while public twins retain exact public metadata."
    },
    {
      "area": "artifact boundary",
      "result": "Secret-bearing artifact expectations are classified before regular-file open, descriptor read, expected-digest comparison, or race pause. Content, digests, serialized paths, Debug paths, and the relative-path accessor are withheld; public artifacts preserve existing identity, budget, race, and special-file controls."
    },
    {
      "area": "retired finite matcher authority",
      "result": "The secret_redaction module and bounded literal/prefix comparison authority were removed. Explicit raw secret placement outside a secret channel may still be rejected as a typed-channel invariant, but it is not used to publish any secret-bearing output or metadata."
    },
    {
      "area": "representative false-pass controls",
      "result": "Focused tests prove public twins and secret-bearing cases for raw, hexadecimal, decimal normalization, case conversion, escaping, encoding, prefix/suffix, two streams, non-UTF8, truncation, failed processes, overlapping secrets, empty-secret rejection, transformed artifacts, serialization and digest absence, pre-open classification, budgets, races, FIFO, and sockets."
    }
  ],
